 "equivalence_evidence": [
  "voxy_world: PalettedBlocks::with_updates fast path compared against the dense repack oracle on random in-palette/new-block/last-occurrence/duplicate updates (chunk.rs tests)",
  "voxy_lighting: new build_light compared byte-for-byte and budget-for-budget (minimal passing budget via bisection) against the previous implementation kept verbatim in the test module",
  "voxy_mesher: greedy mesh compared against the naive per-face oracle on randomized terrain with lamps/glass/water and partial halos (areas, bounds and exact per-cell coverage)",
  "voxy_runtime: partial rebuild of invalidated_derived_chunks merged into the previous derived set equals a full resident rebuild after interior, boundary, corner and multi-chunk edits",
  "voxy_render: welded normals compared against an ordered-map reference on a seam grid; skinned pose validation blends once per vertex with the same accumulation order",
  "physics_voxel: benchmark checksums of water plans, sweep contacts and raycast hits identical before/after; chunk cursor compared against direct sampling across chunk edges",
  "voxy_scene: all 71 scene tests pass; transform-only atomic batches validate in command order and commit through set_locals"
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "shared 4-vCPU cloud host; absolute timings vary run to run, ratios come from alternated runs",
  "scene_scaling rows at 1000 objects showed inconsistent 1.5x swings in both directions across paired runs, including workloads whose code did not change (single-leaf batches); the 10k/100k rows are the stable signal",
  "no GPU in the container: render changes are measured on their CPU parts only; the app's per-edit rebuild saving is derived from rebuild_all_resident scaled by the dirty-chunk ratio, not from a presented-frame measurement",
  "water_tick is unchanged (planner not rewritten); the 4% delta is noise"
 ]
